
# TMR Self-Healing Digital System

## Project Overview
This project demonstrates Triple Modular Redundancy (TMR)
using Verilog HDL. It uses three copies of a logic module
and a majority voter to tolerate a single faulty output.

## Objective
To design and simulate a fault-tolerant digital circuit
that maintains its correct output when one module fails.

## Block Diagram
Input
  |
  +--> Logic Module 1 --+
  +--> Logic Module 2 --+--> Majority Voter --> Output
  +--> Logic Module 3 --+

## Working Principle
1. Three logic modules perform the same AND operation.
2. Each module produces an output.
3. A majority voter selects the value agreed upon by at
   least two outputs.
4. Fault-injection signals can invert individual outputs
   to demonstrate fault masking.

